    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6867" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carpīnus</span></b> , i,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>hornbeam</i> of two species, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Alba or carpinus alone: Carpinus betulus, Linn.; now <i>carpino bianco</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 2, 9, 12, p. 74</span></i> Bip.; <i><span class="en">Col. 5, 7,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 15, 26, § 67</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 18, 30, §
			74</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 43, 83,
				§ 227</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Atra, now called <i>sappino</i>:
			Carpinus ostrya, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			31</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 39, 75, §
		193</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
